---
source: crates/mori-checker/src/tests.rs
description: "Code:\n\nprofile \"moriarty-beta/1\";\nagreement Fields {\n  domain Preview = { id: \"preview\", chain: \"midnight\" };\n  domain Main = { id: \"main\", chain: \"midnight\", network: \"main\", netwrok: \"x\" };\n  account alice = { domain: \"Preview\", id: \"alice\" };\n}\n"
---
mori::check::missing_field

  × This domain is missing the field `network`.
   ╭─[test.mori:3:20]
 2 │ agreement Fields {
 3 │   domain Preview = { id: "preview", chain: "midnight" };
   ·                    ──────────────────┬─────────────────
   ·                                      ╰── needs `network`
 4 │   domain Main = { id: "main", chain: "midnight", network: "main", netwrok: "x" };
   ╰────
  help: A domain takes these fields; `?` marks optional ones:

            { id: string, chain: string, network: string }

mori::check::unknown_field

  × A domain has no field named `netwrok`.
   ╭─[test.mori:4:67]
 3 │   domain Preview = { id: "preview", chain: "midnight" };
 4 │   domain Main = { id: "main", chain: "midnight", network: "main", netwrok: "x" };
   ·                                                                   ───┬───
   ·                                                                      ╰── unknown field
 5 │   account alice = { domain: "Preview", id: "alice" };
   ╰────
  help: Did you mean `network`? A domain takes:

            { id: string, chain: string, network: string }

mori::check::wrong_field

  × The field `domain` of an account must be a domain, but this is a string.
   ╭─[test.mori:5:29]
 4 │   domain Main = { id: "main", chain: "midnight", network: "main", netwrok: "x" };
 5 │   account alice = { domain: "Preview", id: "alice" };
   ·                             ────┬────
   ·                                 ╰── this is a string
 6 │ }
   ╰────
